// FleetScanStatus represents overall outcome of a fleet-scan run from the orchestration layer. Each host of a finished scan has one of three outcomes: it succeeded, it was not assessed (the scan did not reach it: offline when the scan started, or it had not run the scan when the scan stopped waiting; the next scan tries it again), or it failed (the scan reached it and something broke). Hosts that are not eligible (unsupported platform, not managed) take no part. PENDING - workflow kicked off, artifacts not staged yet. RUNNING - artifacts uploading, or hosts are running the script. SUCCESS - every targeted host succeeded. PARTIAL - no host failed, but at least one was not assessed. FAILED - at least one host failed, or no host could be assessed. TIMEOUT - workflow exceeded its overall timeout before all hosts reported. CANCELLED - operator cancelled the scan before it reached a natural terminal state.
